  "body": "**What.** Four `amp_flint_par.py` nodes (K 33, J 1000, 960 bits, `--fit phys --mf 6:12`, 4 processes each) for the candidate second zero of the harmonic-1 Stokes multiplier S1. Node 1.11 was restarted after a worker crash (BrokenPipeError, not memory).\n\n**Why.** Digest, \"In flight right now\" and item 2a. The candidate is item 1 of [notes/HARMONY.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/notes/HARMONY.md). The commands are the 2026-11-07 18:04 UTC entry of [comms.txt](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/comms.txt).\n\n**Acceptance (each can fail).**\n- Each node writes `sigF_w<wf>_K33_J1000.json` and its log into `T155-win2/`.\n- The post gives each node's wall time and the last order's `sigma_err`. A node whose late-order fit shows no plateau is reported as such, not rerun with other options.\n- Raw output goes to a task folder of the raw-data repository (AGENTS.md), and `python3 raw_check.py <folder> PATTERN` passes on it.\n\n**Files.** [solver/inner_amp/amp_flint_par.py](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/solver/inner_amp/amp_flint_par.py), [notes/HARMONY.md](https://github.com/nmoinvaz/choptuik-large-d/blob/main/notes/HARMONY.md)",
